{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the S1 members, serial-read and journal-decoding child at head dcf7e5c73a92c57cfbaf14bbfba314d84bae0b08, tree 4b479784, for child request d5385b16 under amendment ab6bcb38 and review request da1822ce. Verdict: APPROVED for the seven reviewed paths only.\n\n**This verdict does not approve a landing of this head.** The branch carries the 53-path S1 parent, and I reviewed seven paths: `examples/repo-in-ai/members.ts`, `workflow.ts`, `journal.ts`, `test/identities.test.ts`, `test/session.test.mjs`, the note and the manifest. `gs merge` checks which artifacts a landing retires, not whether every path in the commit was reviewed, so the tool may not stop a merge of this commit. Do not merge on this approval. Whole-S1 review at a later exact head and the remaining witnesses come first, as the child and the request state.\n\nI read the note first, then the diff from eece533e.\n\n## The repairs\n\n1. Member readback (`members.ts`). Resolved. The key kind is now separate from the member kind: a person's founding key is `device`, and agents and the checker keep their exact native kinds. All room, party, signer, active-key count, key-to-member, role and controller checks stay. The new case runs actual Membership8 judgments and the maintained enrollment engines, requires the exact four-member result, and refuses a cross-bound key at the read boundary. Directory, Rules and Destination are labelled stand-ins.\n2. Serial reads (`workflow.ts`). Resolved. The three sibling reads run in order on one Session, whose busy guard is unchanged. The test uses the actual Session, signed read-session requests and private proof writes, and it failed naturally before the change.\n3. Journal decoding (`journal.ts`). Resolved.\n   - The reader now takes the `{seq, hash, bytes}` rows that the record returns. It checks closed keys, the sequence, the byte bound, the raw-byte hash, a strict parse, `isEntry`, canonical bytes, `entryHash`, identity and the previous-hash chain, all before `applyEntry`.\n   - The head must stay the same across pages, and the journal must close at it. The page count, the 512-entry bound and the cursor checks stay.\n   - The test rewrites the wire to exercise these refusals through the real transport and MCP record.\n\nFailed and inconclusive runs keep their outcomes in the note. The first control stays inconclusive, the second distinguishes, and the first diagnostic's omission of the retained-definition route isn't presented as a provider cause. The 404's site stays unknown, and the note says so.\n\n## The gates\n\n- The gate at 52571fc2, tree 4c3d96d0, passes all five stages. Its receipt exits 0 with complete capture and the same source before and after. Plain passes 3,163 with one skip and Native 859 with two skips.\n- The gates at 8f91eaf6 and earlier stay historical, as ruling 733ed1b4 says. The serial checkpoint was not gated, and the note says that too.\n- From 52571fc2 to the head, only the note and the manifest change.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The review worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5068dab4 gives 970361ad, with no conflict.\n- The seven artifacts are all at this head, and the note is the commitment's report.\n- I ran the owning files once each, in the S1 worktree at the tested source 52571fc2: `identities.test.ts`, 7 of 7; `session.test.mjs`, 5 of 5. That worktree stayed clean.\n- The evidence verifies. The directory has 2,625 files and 202,029,694 bytes, its `SHA256SUMS` has digest 24bb3e72 and reruns clean, and no file is unlisted or writable. All 327 rows of the compact manifest, SHA-256 1c177831, match by size and SHA-256.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 764 links, 0 broken. check-notes from eece533e: 0 warnings. check-commit-messages from eece533e: 4 checked, 0 flagged.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The stand-in `Session` in the members case throws on any write, which is good, but the Directory, Rules and Destination context is scripted, so the case shows no native room read. The live members check supplies that.\n2. Fork readiness stays false in the scratch room because of an unknown head outcome (fold 9, fork creating). The note reports this as an observation, and request f0bdea6f owns the recovery. It's outside this child.\n3. The note still uses \"Root\" for the builder.\n\n## Architecture\n\nAll three repairs stay in the example's helper, over the maintained engines, and change no CLI engine, wire format, cohort or kernel. Approved for the seven paths.\n\n## Security\n\nThe journal reader verifies every row before folding it, which is stronger than what it replaces. The member check keeps every authority binding. No credential moves. Approved for the seven paths.\n\n## Simplification\n\nEach repair is small, and the journal check uses the maintained helpers. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved for the seven paths.\n- Security: approved for the seven paths.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the three repairs, their regressions and controls, the passing gate with a documents-only tail, and the evidence all hold.\n- Still open: the remaining scratch witnesses, the real room, and exact whole-S1 review before any landing. This verdict claims none of them.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b31b5b0a623624a1ed8a15704e75a5e1c902f35b","binding":"assigned","head":"dcf7e5c73a92c57cfbaf14bbfba314d84bae0b08","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a182feabd7c2be94458586e54f2424223ff1e1ef\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ae019fe219fb6ce1aa56b974ced8db5f8048c6d1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a182feabd7c2be94458586e54f2424223ff1e1ef","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:182044ba2370